## HOLDS
- Datasec / Security Composer only; if any output shows another client's material, stop and disclose its shape. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra tenant, Graph, ssh, no migration against any hosted database. **No HTTP to any hosted or production site or the demo site** (the tests are in-process and in an internal-only Docker network; the only listener you may start is on `127.0.0.1` inside 9440-9449, and none is expected). Network: `git fetch` of explicit refspecs into YOUR scratch clone, `gh api -X GET` under `GH_CONFIG_DIR='<project>/4_Credentials/.gh-config'`, Jira GET as C7b allows, nothing else. `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh api -X POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE` are forbidden. Never dismiss an alert. No decision-queue tool in any form, no scoreboard, no Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool.
- **Git in the project repo: READ verbs only** (`--no-optional-locks`: `ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`); `fetch`, `worktree`, the legacy 3-argument `merge-tree`, `checkout`, `apply`, `merge`, `gc`, `worktree prune` only inside `.tools/b593/repo` and `.tools/wt-b593-*`. No git verb in the project root (the records repo). **Forbidden everywhere: `merge-tree --write-tree`.** Never fetch, check out, worktree-add or write in `2_Project_Files` itself or any other Composer tree.
- **The HP-NDA and real-document hold:** no HP Restricted document to any AI tool; never open `HP Reporting and Docs/`, any SOW, or `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/` contents, nor Tuesday's `inbound/` folders. The Essential Eight SOW text for the unit step is passed ONLY as Q-2 rules: stat it with `[ -f ]`, bind it read-only into a `--network none` container, never open, print, grep, hash to screen or quote it. Every scratch row, tenant and fixture is synthetic. Secrets only as environment, never on argv; never open `4_Credentials/.env` except the NAME test and the Jira GET; never open `3_Access_Keys/`.
- **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -D`, `docker volume rm`, `down -v`, `prune`, `image rm`, `update-ref -d`): quarantine to `.tools/b593/quarantine/`; the one exception is your own throwaway `pc-b593-*` db container, anonymous volume and internal network, by exact name after the log is saved. **Never `cd`** (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain spaces and `!`; a word-split path wrote stray files into a project root before: every path in a redirect, a marker, a log line and a script is single-quoted or in an array; create none, touch none); where `docker`, `node` or `npm` needs a cwd, set it with Python `subprocess(cwd=...)` or `bash -c` and say so; write `${VAR}:path`; multi-step chains under `bash -c '...'` or a QUOTED heredoc; no unquoted word starting with `=` in command position (use `----` as a separator); bash, not zsh, for loops; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count (macOS grep has no `-P`: use `-E`); `python3 -I` for anything that reads a file you did not write. Print `git status --short` of the project root before your first step and after your last.
